{
  "metadata": { "name": "Option Greeks", "language_info": { "name": "JavaScipt", "version": "8.0" } },
  "jsnbversion": "v0.1",
  "cells": [
    { "code": "# Voltrix Tests — `/options/greeks`\n", "status": "", "output": "<h1>Voltrix Tests — <code>/options/greeks</code></h1>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "const BASE = 'http://localhost:8000/v2';\n\nasync function post(path, body) {\n  const res = await fetch(`${BASE}${path}`, {\n    method: 'POST',\n    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    body: JSON.stringify(body),\n  });\n  return res.json();\n}", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "---\n\n## 1. Analytical Greeks — Interactive\n", "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>1. Analytical Greeks — Interactive</h2>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "//>html\n<div>\n  <label>Type <select id='gk-type'><option value='call'>call</option><option value='put'>put</option></select></label>\n  <label>Method <select id='gk-method'><option value='analytic'>analytic</option><option value='finite_difference'>finite_difference</option></select></label>\n  <label>Spot <input id='gk-spot' type='number' value='100'></label>\n  <label>Strike <input id='gk-strike' type='number' value='100'></label>\n  <label>Rate <input id='gk-rate' type='number' value='0.05' step='0.01'></label>\n  <label>Settlement Date <input id='gk-settle' type='date' value='2026-04-01'></label>\n  <label>Expiry Date <input id='gk-expiry' type='date' value='2027-04-01'></label>\n  <label>Vol (σ) <input id='gk-vol' type='number' value='0.2' step='0.01'></label>\n  <label>Bump Size <input id='gk-bump' type='number' value='0.01' step='0.005'></label>\n</div>", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "const result = await post('/options/greeks', {\n  model: 'black_scholes',\n  option_type:     document.getElementById('gk-type').value,\n  spot:            parseFloat(document.getElementById('gk-spot').value),\n  strike:          parseFloat(document.getElementById('gk-strike').value),\n  rate:            parseFloat(document.getElementById('gk-rate').value),\n  settlement_date: document.getElementById('gk-settle').value,\n  expiry_date:     document.getElementById('gk-expiry').value,\n  volatility:      parseFloat(document.getElementById('gk-vol').value),\n  method:          document.getElementById('gk-method').value,\n  bump_size:       parseFloat(document.getElementById('gk-bump').value),\n  include_insights: true,\n});\nscrib.show('Δ delta:  ' + result.delta);\nscrib.show('Γ gamma:  ' + result.gamma);\nscrib.show('ν vega:   ' + result.vega  + '  (' + result.units.vega + ')');\nscrib.show('Θ theta:  ' + result.theta + '  (' + result.units.theta + ')');\nscrib.show('ρ rho:    ' + result.rho);\nscrib.show(result.interpretation);", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "---\n\n## 2. Analytic vs Finite Difference Comparison\n", "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>2. Analytic vs Finite Difference Comparison</h2>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "//>html\n<div>\n  <label>Spot <input id='cmp-spot' type='number' value='100'></label>\n  <label>Strike <input id='cmp-strike' type='number' value='105'></label>\n  <label>Vol <input id='cmp-vol' type='number' value='0.2' step='0.01'></label>\n  <label>Settlement Date <input id='cmp-settle' type='date' value='2026-04-01'></label>\n  <label>Expiry Date <input id='cmp-expiry' type='date' value='2027-04-01'></label>\n</div>", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "const shared = {\n  model: 'black_scholes', option_type: 'call', rate: 0.05,\n  spot:            parseFloat(document.getElementById('cmp-spot').value),\n  strike:          parseFloat(document.getElementById('cmp-strike').value),\n  volatility:      parseFloat(document.getElementById('cmp-vol').value),\n  settlement_date: document.getElementById('cmp-settle').value,\n  expiry_date:     document.getElementById('cmp-expiry').value,\n};\nconst [analytic, numerical] = await Promise.all([\n  post('/options/greeks', { ...shared, method: 'analytic' }),\n  post('/options/greeks', { ...shared, method: 'finite_difference', bump_size: 0.01 }),\n]);\nscrib.show('Greek  | Analytic     | Numerical    | Diff');\n['delta','gamma','vega','theta','rho'].forEach(g => {\n  const diff = Math.abs(analytic[g] - numerical[g]);\n  scrib.show(g.padEnd(6) + ' | ' + String(analytic[g]).padEnd(12) + ' | ' + String(numerical[g]).padEnd(12) + ' | ' + diff.toFixed(7));\n});", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "---\n\n## 3. Put-Call Parity on Greeks\n\nΔ(call) − Δ(put) = e^(−qT) ≈ 1 for q=0. Γ and ν must be identical for call and put.\n", "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>3. Put-Call Parity on Greeks</h2>\n<p>Δ(call) − Δ(put) = e^(−qT) ≈ 1 for q=0. Γ and ν must be identical for call and put.</p>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "const S = parseFloat(document.getElementById('cmp-spot').value);\nconst K = parseFloat(document.getElementById('cmp-strike').value);\nconst v = parseFloat(document.getElementById('cmp-vol').value);\nconst settle = document.getElementById('cmp-settle').value;\nconst expiry = document.getElementById('cmp-expiry').value;\n\nconst base = { model: 'black_scholes', rate: 0.05, spot: S, strike: K,\n               volatility: v, settlement_date: settle, expiry_date: expiry, method: 'analytic' };\nconst [call, put] = await Promise.all([\n  post('/options/greeks', { ...base, option_type: 'call' }),\n  post('/options/greeks', { ...base, option_type: 'put' }),\n]);\nscrib.show('Δ(call) − Δ(put): ' + (call.delta - put.delta).toFixed(6) + '  (expect ≈ 1.0)');\nscrib.show('Γ equal: ' + (call.gamma === put.gamma) + '  ' + call.gamma);\nscrib.show('ν equal: ' + (call.vega  === put.vega)  + '  ' + call.vega);", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "---\n\n## 4. Greeks with Matrix Vol Surface\n\nA matrix vol surface forces automatic finite-difference computation.\n", "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>4. Greeks with Matrix Vol Surface</h2>\n<p>A matrix vol surface forces automatic finite-difference computation.</p>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "//>html\n<div>\n  <label>Query Strike <input id='surf-gk-k' type='number' value='100'></label>\n  <label>Settlement Date <input id='surf-gk-settle' type='date' value='2026-04-01'></label>\n  <label>Expiry Date <input id='surf-gk-expiry' type='date' value='2026-10-01'></label>\n</div>", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "const result = await post('/options/greeks', {\n  model: 'black_scholes', option_type: 'call', spot: 100, rate: 0.05,\n  strike:          parseFloat(document.getElementById('surf-gk-k').value),\n  settlement_date: document.getElementById('surf-gk-settle').value,\n  expiry_date:     document.getElementById('surf-gk-expiry').value,\n  volatility: {\n    surface_type: 'matrix',\n    data: {\n      strikes: [90, 100, 110], maturities: [0.5, 1.0],\n      vol_matrix: [[0.25, 0.24], [0.20, 0.19], [0.22, 0.21]],\n    },\n    interpolation: 'bilinear', extrapolation: 'flat',\n  },\n  method: 'analytic', include_insights: true,\n});\nscrib.show(result);\nscrib.show('σ interpolated: ' + result.volatility_used.value + ' from ' + result.volatility_used.source);", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "---\n\n## 5. Delta vs Spot — Sensitivity Curve\n\nSweep spot from 70 to 130 and observe how delta and gamma evolve.\n", "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>5. Delta vs Spot — Sensitivity Curve</h2>\n<p>Sweep spot from 70 to 130 and observe how delta and gamma evolve.</p>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "//>html\n<div>\n  <label>Strike <input id='dlt-k' type='number' value='100'></label>\n  <label>Vol <input id='dlt-vol' type='number' value='0.2' step='0.01'></label>\n  <label>Settlement Date <input id='dlt-settle' type='date' value='2026-04-01'></label>\n  <label>Expiry Date <input id='dlt-expiry' type='date' value='2027-04-01'></label>\n</div>", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "const K      = parseFloat(document.getElementById('dlt-k').value);\nconst vol    = parseFloat(document.getElementById('dlt-vol').value);\nconst settle = document.getElementById('dlt-settle').value;\nconst expiry = document.getElementById('dlt-expiry').value;\n\nconst spots = [70, 80, 90, 95, 100, 105, 110, 120, 130];\nconst results = await Promise.all(spots.map(S =>\n  post('/options/greeks', {\n    model: 'black_scholes', option_type: 'call',\n    spot: S, strike: K, rate: 0.05,\n    settlement_date: settle, expiry_date: expiry,\n    volatility: vol, method: 'analytic',\n  })\n));\nscrib.show('Spot | Delta  | Gamma');\nspots.forEach((S, i) =>\n  scrib.show(S.toString().padStart(4) + ' | ' + results[i].delta.toFixed(4) + ' | ' + results[i].gamma.toFixed(5))\n);", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "---\n\n## 6. SABR Greeks — Interactive\n\nSABR surface forces finite-difference. Delta and vega correctly account for the SABR smile\nshape through bump-and-reprice.\n", "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>6. SABR Greeks — Interactive</h2>\n<p>SABR surface auto-forces finite-difference. Greeks include smile-shape sensitivity.</p>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "//>html\n<div>\n  <label>Type <select id='sgk-type'><option value='call'>call</option><option value='put'>put</option></select></label>\n  <label>Spot <input id='sgk-spot' type='number' value='100'></label>\n  <label>Strike <input id='sgk-strike' type='number' value='105'></label>\n  <label>Rate <input id='sgk-rate' type='number' value='0.05' step='0.01'></label>\n  <label>Settlement Date <input id='sgk-settle' type='date' value='2026-04-01'></label>\n  <label>Expiry Date <input id='sgk-expiry' type='date' value='2027-04-01'></label>\n  <label>α <input id='sgk-alpha' type='number' value='0.3' step='0.05'></label>\n  <label>β <input id='sgk-beta' type='number' value='0.5' step='0.1'></label>\n  <label>ρ <input id='sgk-rho' type='number' value='-0.3' step='0.1'></label>\n  <label>ν <input id='sgk-nu' type='number' value='0.4' step='0.05'></label>\n</div>", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "const result = await post('/options/greeks', {\n  model: 'black_scholes',\n  option_type:     document.getElementById('sgk-type').value,\n  spot:            parseFloat(document.getElementById('sgk-spot').value),\n  strike:          parseFloat(document.getElementById('sgk-strike').value),\n  rate:            parseFloat(document.getElementById('sgk-rate').value),\n  settlement_date: document.getElementById('sgk-settle').value,\n  expiry_date:     document.getElementById('sgk-expiry').value,\n  method: 'analytic',  // will be auto-overridden to finite_difference\n  volatility: {\n    surface_type: 'sabr',\n    other_params: {\n      alpha: parseFloat(document.getElementById('sgk-alpha').value),\n      beta:  parseFloat(document.getElementById('sgk-beta').value),\n      rho:   parseFloat(document.getElementById('sgk-rho').value),\n      nu:    parseFloat(document.getElementById('sgk-nu').value),\n    },\n  },\n});\nscrib.show('SABR σ resolved: ' + result.volatility_used.value);\nscrib.show('Δ delta:  ' + result.delta);\nscrib.show('Γ gamma:  ' + result.gamma);\nscrib.show('ν vega:   ' + result.vega  + '  (' + result.units.vega + ')');\nscrib.show('Θ theta:  ' + result.theta + '  (' + result.units.theta + ')');\nscrib.show('ρ rho:    ' + result.rho);", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "---\n\n## 7. SABR Greeks — Delta Skew (call vs put)\n\nWith SABR skew (ρ ≠ 0), Δ(call) − Δ(put) still ≈ 1 (put-call parity on delta holds).\n", "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>7. SABR Greeks — Delta Skew (call vs put)</h2>\n<p>Δ(call) − Δ(put) ≈ 1 must hold even with a skewed SABR surface.</p>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "const sabrP = { alpha: 0.3, beta: 0.5, rho: -0.5, nu: 0.4 };\nconst base = {\n  model: 'black_scholes', spot: 100, strike: 100, rate: 0.05,\n  settlement_date: '2026-04-01', expiry_date: '2027-04-01',\n  volatility: { surface_type: 'sabr', other_params: sabrP },\n};\nconst [call, put] = await Promise.all([\n  post('/options/greeks', { ...base, option_type: 'call' }),\n  post('/options/greeks', { ...base, option_type: 'put' }),\n]);\nscrib.show('SABR σ at ATM:    ' + call.volatility_used.value);\nscrib.show('Δ(call):          ' + call.delta);\nscrib.show('Δ(put):           ' + put.delta);\nscrib.show('Δ(call) − Δ(put): ' + (call.delta - put.delta).toFixed(6) + '  (expect ≈ 1.0)');", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "---\n\n## 8. Heston Greeks — Interactive\n\nHeston always uses finite-difference. Vega = ∂Price/∂σ₀ per 1% change in σ₀ = √v0.\nThis measures sensitivity to the initial vol level, not a flat-vol bump.\n", "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>8. Heston Greeks — Interactive</h2>\n<p>Heston always uses finite-difference. Vega = ∂P/∂σ₀ per 1% change in initial vol √v0.</p>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "//>html\n<div>\n  <label>Type <select id='hgk-type'><option value='call'>call</option><option value='put'>put</option></select></label>\n  <label>Spot <input id='hgk-spot' type='number' value='100'></label>\n  <label>Strike <input id='hgk-strike' type='number' value='105'></label>\n  <label>Rate <input id='hgk-rate' type='number' value='0.05' step='0.01'></label>\n  <label>Settlement Date <input id='hgk-settle' type='date' value='2026-04-01'></label>\n  <label>Expiry Date <input id='hgk-expiry' type='date' value='2027-04-01'></label>\n  <label>v0 <input id='hgk-v0' type='number' value='0.04' step='0.01'></label>\n  <label>κ (kappa) <input id='hgk-kappa' type='number' value='2.0' step='0.5'></label>\n  <label>θ (theta) <input id='hgk-theta' type='number' value='0.04' step='0.01'></label>\n  <label>σᵥ (sigma_v) <input id='hgk-sv' type='number' value='0.3' step='0.05'></label>\n  <label>ρ (rho) <input id='hgk-rho' type='number' value='-0.7' step='0.1'></label>\n</div>", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "const hp = {\n  v0:      parseFloat(document.getElementById('hgk-v0').value),\n  kappa:   parseFloat(document.getElementById('hgk-kappa').value),\n  theta:   parseFloat(document.getElementById('hgk-theta').value),\n  sigma_v: parseFloat(document.getElementById('hgk-sv').value),\n  rho:     parseFloat(document.getElementById('hgk-rho').value),\n};\nconst result = await post('/options/greeks', {\n  model: 'heston',\n  option_type:     document.getElementById('hgk-type').value,\n  spot:            parseFloat(document.getElementById('hgk-spot').value),\n  strike:          parseFloat(document.getElementById('hgk-strike').value),\n  rate:            parseFloat(document.getElementById('hgk-rate').value),\n  settlement_date: document.getElementById('hgk-settle').value,\n  expiry_date:     document.getElementById('hgk-expiry').value,\n  volatility: { surface_type: 'heston', other_params: hp },\n});\nscrib.show('Ref σ₀ = √v0: ' + result.volatility_used.value);\nscrib.show('Δ delta:  ' + result.delta);\nscrib.show('Γ gamma:  ' + result.gamma);\nscrib.show('ν vega:   ' + result.vega  + '  (per 1% change in σ₀)');\nscrib.show('Θ theta:  ' + result.theta + '  (' + result.units.theta + ')');\nscrib.show('ρ rho:    ' + result.rho);", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "---\n\n## 9. Heston Greeks — Put-Call Parity on Delta\n\nΔ(call) − Δ(put) ≈ 1 must hold for Heston as for any model.\n", "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>9. Heston Greeks — Put-Call Parity on Delta</h2>\n<p>Δ(call) − Δ(put) ≈ e^(−qT) ≈ 1 for q=0.</p>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "const hp   = { v0: 0.04, kappa: 2.0, theta: 0.04, sigma_v: 0.3, rho: -0.7 };\nconst base = {\n  model: 'heston', spot: 100, strike: 100, rate: 0.05,\n  settlement_date: '2026-04-01', expiry_date: '2027-04-01',\n  volatility: { surface_type: 'heston', other_params: hp },\n};\nconst [call, put] = await Promise.all([\n  post('/options/greeks', { ...base, option_type: 'call' }),\n  post('/options/greeks', { ...base, option_type: 'put' }),\n]);\nscrib.show('Δ(call):          ' + call.delta);\nscrib.show('Δ(put):           ' + put.delta);\nscrib.show('Δ(call) − Δ(put): ' + (call.delta - put.delta).toFixed(6) + '  (expect ≈ 1.0)');\nscrib.show('Γ equal:          ' + (call.gamma === put.gamma) + '  ' + call.gamma);", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "---\n\n## 10. Heston Greeks — Delta vs Spot Sweep\n\nSweep spot from 70 to 130 to see Heston delta and gamma profile.\nWith negative ρ the delta profile shifts compared to flat-vol Black-Scholes.\n", "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>10. Heston Greeks — Delta vs Spot Sweep</h2>\n<p>Negative ρ distorts the delta profile vs flat-vol BS.</p>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "const hp     = { v0: 0.04, kappa: 2.0, theta: 0.04, sigma_v: 0.3, rho: -0.7 };\nconst spots  = [70, 80, 90, 95, 100, 105, 110, 120, 130];\nconst results = await Promise.all(spots.map(S =>\n  post('/options/greeks', {\n    model: 'heston', option_type: 'call',\n    spot: S, strike: 100, rate: 0.05,\n    settlement_date: '2026-04-01', expiry_date: '2027-04-01',\n    volatility: { surface_type: 'heston', other_params: hp },\n  })\n));\nscrib.show('Spot | Δ delta  | Γ gamma');\nspots.forEach((S, i) =>\n  scrib.show(S.toString().padStart(4) + ' | ' +\n    results[i].delta.toFixed(5) + ' | ' +\n    results[i].gamma.toFixed(5))\n);", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "---\n\n## 11. Heston Vega — v0 Sensitivity Check\n\nVega should be positive (higher initial vol → higher option price). Verify by comparing\nprices at v0±Δv and checking the finite-difference result matches the greeks endpoint.\n", "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>11. Heston Vega — v0 Sensitivity Check</h2>\n<p>Verify that Heston vega (∂P/∂σ₀) is consistent with direct price bumps on v0.</p>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "const v0  = 0.04;\nconst dv0 = 0.01;  // bump σ₀ by 1% → v0 changes from (√v0)² to (√v0 + 0.01)²\nconst sig0     = Math.sqrt(v0);\nconst v0_up    = Math.pow(sig0 + dv0, 2);\nconst v0_dn    = Math.pow(Math.max(sig0 - dv0, 0.001), 2);\nconst hpBase   = { kappa: 2.0, theta: 0.04, sigma_v: 0.3, rho: -0.7 };\nconst reqBase  = {\n  model: 'heston', option_type: 'call',\n  spot: 100, strike: 105, rate: 0.05,\n  settlement_date: '2026-04-01', expiry_date: '2027-04-01',\n};\n\nconst [base, pUp, pDn, greeks] = await Promise.all([\n  post('/options/price',  { ...reqBase, volatility: { surface_type: 'heston', other_params: { ...hpBase, v0 } } }),\n  post('/options/price',  { ...reqBase, volatility: { surface_type: 'heston', other_params: { ...hpBase, v0: v0_up } } }),\n  post('/options/price',  { ...reqBase, volatility: { surface_type: 'heston', other_params: { ...hpBase, v0: v0_dn } } }),\n  post('/options/greeks', { ...reqBase, volatility: { surface_type: 'heston', other_params: { ...hpBase, v0 } } }),\n]);\nconst fdVega = (pUp.price - pDn.price) / (v0_up - v0_dn) * 2 * dv0 * 0.01;\nscrib.show('Price at v0:     ' + base.price);\nscrib.show('Price at v0+:    ' + pUp.price + '  (σ₀=' + (sig0+dv0).toFixed(3) + ')');\nscrib.show('Price at v0−:    ' + pDn.price + '  (σ₀=' + (sig0-dv0).toFixed(3) + ')');\nscrib.show('FD vega (manual):  ' + fdVega.toFixed(6));\nscrib.show('Greeks endpoint:   ' + greeks.vega + '  (per 1% σ₀ change)');\nscrib.show('Vega is positive:  ' + (greeks.vega > 0));", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" },
    { "code": "---\n\n## 12. SVI Greeks — Smile-Aware Finite Difference\n\nSVI surface forces finite-difference. Because the implied vol depends on K (smile),\nthe delta differs from flat-vol delta.\n", "status": "", "output": "<hr>\n<h2>12. SVI Greeks — Smile-Aware Finite Difference</h2>\n<p>SVI surface forces FD. Delta includes the smile-adjusted vol change as spot moves.</p>\n", "type": "html" },
    { "code": "const sviP = { a: 0.04, b: 0.2, rho: -0.3, m: 0.0, sigma: 0.3 };\nconst base = {\n  model: 'black_scholes', option_type: 'call',\n  spot: 100, strike: 105, rate: 0.05,\n  settlement_date: '2026-04-01', expiry_date: '2027-04-01',\n};\nconst [sviGreeks, flatGreeks] = await Promise.all([\n  post('/options/greeks', { ...base,\n    volatility: { surface_type: 'svi', other_params: sviP } }),\n  post('/options/greeks', { ...base, volatility: 0.2 }),  // flat vol for comparison\n]);\nscrib.show('--- SVI (smile-aware FD) ---');\nscrib.show('σ: ' + sviGreeks.volatility_used.value);\nscrib.show('Δ: ' + sviGreeks.delta + '  Γ: ' + sviGreeks.gamma + '  ν: ' + sviGreeks.vega);\nscrib.show('--- Flat vol 0.20 (analytic) ---');\nscrib.show('Δ: ' + flatGreeks.delta + '  Γ: ' + flatGreeks.gamma + '  ν: ' + flatGreeks.vega);", "status": "", "output": "", "type": "code" }
  ],
  "source": "https://github.com/gopi-suvanam/scribbler",
  "run_on_load": false
}
